month month 13 is not between 1 and 12
year year 0 is not between 1 and 9999
leap day 29 is not between 1 and 28: February 2026 has 28 days
parse range "2026-13-01" is not a valid date: month 13 is not between 1 and 12
parse shape "25/09/2026" is not a date written as YYYY-MM-DD, such as 2026-09-25
past 9999 year 10000 is not between 1 and 9999
month past 9999 year 10000 is not between 1 and 9999
date and time day 30 is not between 1 and 28: February 2026 has 28 days
hour past 9999 year 10000 is not between 1 and 9999
hour hour 24 is not between 0 and 23
minute minute 60 is not between 0 and 59
nanosecond nanosecond -1 is not between 0 and 999999999
parse shape "7:30" is not a time written as HH:MM or HH:MM:SS, such as 14:30
parse range "12:61" is not a valid time: minute 61 is not between 0 and 59
date and time text "2026-09-25T24:00" is not a valid date and time: hour 24 is not between 0 and 23
date and time shape "2026-09-25" is not a date and time written as YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS, such as 2026-09-25T14:30:00
a Duration cannot be divided by zero
DateTimeError a Duration cannot be divided by a zero Duration
after 9999 this moment is after 9999-12-31T23:59:59.999999999Z, the latest an Instant can be
before 1 this moment is before 0001-01-01T00:00:00Z, the earliest an Instant can be
no offset "2026-09-25T14:30:00" has no Z or offset, so it could be any moment: add Z for UTC, or read it with DateTime.parse
moment shape "2026-09-25T14:30Q" is not a moment written as YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS with Z or an offset, such as 2026-09-25T14:30:00Z
moment range "2026-09-25T14:61:00Z" is not a valid moment: minute 61 is not between 0 and 59
zone name "Mars/Olympus" is not a time zone Emerald knows: use an IANA name such as "Europe/Paris", "UTC", or an offset such as "+05:30"
minute sign minutes 30 must be between -59 and 59, with the same sign as hours -3: write minutes: -30 instead
offset size an offset of 19 hours is not between -18 and 18
`Program.sleep` cannot pause for a negative Duration
